course: dictionary
lesson: 6902
title: Own: having it as yours
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word own can be a verb or an adjective. As a verb, to own something means to have it as yours: someone who owns a bike has that bike. Owns, owned and owning are other forms of the verb.
explain: After my, your, his, her, its, our or their, own is an adjective meaning belonging to that one only. «A parent can help you get your own library card» means a card that is yours and nobody else's.
explain: Own has other meanings too. «On your own» means alone, or without help. «To own up» means to admit you did something wrong. The words around own show you which meaning is right.
explain: Check by swapping. In «British Sign Language is a full language with its own grammar», you could put «its» in place of «own» and the sentence still makes sense. So own here means belonging to it. Always test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Own can be a verb: to own, owns, owned, owning.
fact: After my, your, his, her, its, our or their, «own» means belonging to that one only.
fact: «On your own» means alone, or without help.
fact: «To own up» means to admit you did something wrong.
fact: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle» shows that the whistle belongs to one dolphin.
exercise: «Borrowing books from the public library is free, and a parent can help you get your own library card.» What does own mean here? | *Belonging to you, and nobody else | Borrowed from a friend | Made by a parent | Lost and found
exercise: Nadia says, «I can make my lunch on my own.» What does on my own mean? | Very hungry | *Alone, without help | In a hurry | With a big group of friends
exercise: «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language with its own grammar.» Copy the word that shows the grammar belongs to BSL. | grammar | language | *own | full
test: «To own up» means what? | To run fast | *To admit you did something wrong | To own a pet | To buy something new
test: Ella ___ a red bike, so she can ride it whenever she likes. | owned | *owns | own | owning
exam: In «A main clause makes sense on its own», what does on its own mean? | *Able to stand alone as a complete sentence | Angrily | Very quietly | Owned by a teacher
